        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d15304bf-87d3-5abd-bae6-759a96399361",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Dhool, Ranja\n- People: Dharani, Vikram, Jyothika, Reemma Sen, Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala, Pasupathy, Kennedy John Victor, Sudesh Wasantha Peiris, Sunil T. Fernando\n- Companies: Sunil T. Films\n- Awards: Filmfare Awards, National Film Award, Tamil Nadu State Film Award, Honorary Doctorate\n- Organizations: People's University of Milan\n- Topics: Tamil cinema, Sinhala cinema, film remakes\n\nFacts:\n- Dhool is a 2003 Indian Tamil-language action masala film directed by Dharani.\n- Dhool stars Vikram, Jyothika, and Reemma Sen in the lead roles.\n- Dhool features Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala, and Pasupathy in supporting roles.\n- Kennedy John Victor is professionally known as Vikram or Chiyaan Vikram.\n- Vikram is an Indian film actor who predominantly appears in Tamil-language films.\n- Vikram has won seven Filmfare Awards, one National Film Award, and one Tamil Nadu State Film Award.\n- In May 2011, the People's University of Milan awarded Vikram an Honorary Doctorate.\n- Ranja is a 2014 Sri Lankan Sinhala action thriller film directed by Sudesh Wasantha Peiris.\n- Sunil T. Fernando produced Ranja for Sunil T. Films.\n- Ranja is a remake of the 2003 Tamil-language film Dhool.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cf61e359-e178-5f29-aa71-7f5a47960ded",
        "text": "Page: Dhool. Sentence: Dhool (English: Super ) is a 2003 Indian Tamil-language action masala film directed by Dharani.\nPage: Dhool. Sentence: The film featured Vikram, Jyothika and Reemma Sen in the lead roles, while Vivek, Sayaji Shinde, Telangana Sakunthala and Pasupathy among others play supporting roles.\nPage: Vikram (actor). Sentence: Kennedy John Victor, known professionally as Vikram or Chiyaan Vikram, is an Indian film actor who predominantly appears in Tamil language films and has won seven Filmfare Awards as well as one National Film Award and Tamil Nadu State Film Award amongst other recognitions and was awarded an Honorary Doctorate by the People's University of Milan in May 2011.\nPage: Ranja. Sentence: Ranja (Sinhalese: \"රන්ජා\" ) is a 2014 Sri Lankan Sinhala action thriller film directed by Sudesh Wasantha Peiris and produced by Sunil T. Fernando for Sunil T. Films.It was the remake of 2003 Tamil language film Dhool.",
